verified: |
  obs doctor mcp-interpreter check + --json fix (2026-08-17, PRs #96/#97, merged to dev): fixed
  the Claude Desktop MCP outage this session — a Homebrew python@3.14 patch bump (3.14.6→3.14.7)
  deleted a version-pinned Cellar path the obsidian-ops MCP entry was hardcoded to, and `obs
  doctor` reported all-pass throughout. Added `mcp-interpreter` to the `mcp` layer: fails on a
  dead/non-executable/unresolvable interpreter, warns when it resolves but is pinned to a
  version-specific Homebrew Cellar path (incl. revision-suffixed, e.g. `3.14.6_1`) — the exact
  fragility that broke. Adversarial review (opencode) caught a crash bug (non-string `command`
  value raised an uncaught TypeError) and the revision-suffix regex gap before merge; both fixed
  with regression tests. Also fixed a separate pre-existing bug found along the way: `obs doctor
  --json` crashed on every layer (`UnboundLocalError` from a shadowed local `import json`
  elsewhere in `obs_cli.py`'s `main()`), spun off as PR #97. Added e2e (real subprocess,
  `E2E=1`-gated) + dogfood (in-process via `obs_cli.main()`) coverage for both. Tests: 603 pytest
  (non-e2e) + 138 e2e collected.
  Issue #85 (diagnostics/installer hardening) + Issue #86 (vault reorg path migration) — completed on dev 2026-07-11. Issue #85: vault nesting guard (db_manager), failed_paths persistence (vault_scanner), iCloud per-vault offload warnings, targeted diagnose layers, Claude Desktop MCP auto-config (install.sh + scripts/configure_mcp.py), global verbose flag fix. Issue #86: migrated board path from retired 00_meta to Engineering/_ACTION-BOARD.md (board.py + test_board.py), config/example.project_map.json already uses Engineering/packages/ + Research/. Tests: 764 pytest + 69 Jest passing.
  Obsidian-sync validation (2026-07-12, bf5dd59→52e5a46): Added JSON Schema for .flow/obsidian-sync.yml, 6 doctor checks (missing, schema, stale, vault-root, pair-duplicate, pair-identity), `obs flow init` command (interactive + non-interactive modes), updated savant:restore and craft:recap hooks. Tests: 764 pytest + 69 Jest passing (58 new tests: 23 unit + 19 dogfood + 16 e2e). Docs: CLAUDE.md, refcard, cli-reference, testing overview updated. Commands: 64 (was 63). Adversarial review: 17 fixes (critical bugs, security, correctness, design) — atomic write, path traversal blocking, backup before overwrite, corrupted YAML handling.
